From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:12:21 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] drm/apple: Fix no display on a T6050 with more than one
 DCP

On the M5 Ultra Mac Studio (J775D) no output came up: not HDMI, not
the USB-C displays, so there was no desktop and no HDMI audio.

The boot loader has one boot framebuffer to hand over, so it gives the
"framebuffer" memory region to one DCP only. dcp_firmware_metadata_v27()
required that region on every 27.x DCP, so each other DCP failed to bind
with -EINVAL. The display driver binds all DCPs or none, so that
failure also took down the DCP that had the region.

A DCP without a boot framebuffer is a normal state, not an error. Bind
it without the region; the existing size check (dfb_region_size 0)
refuses its default-framebuffer requests.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Queisser <funkzy@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit 95bcc467a27859c7739af36b9582fd23419a69df)
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
index fad745267532..380c31ab8669 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp.c
@@ -5153,10 +5153,22 @@ static int dcp_firmware_metadata_v27(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 	struct resource resource;
 	int clocks, index, ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * The framebuffer region is the one the boot loader scanned out of; it
+	 * backs the firmware's default framebuffer.  An external processor the
+	 * boot loader drove no display from (T6050's dcpext4, the HDMI port's)
+	 * has none: it binds without one, and its default-framebuffer requests
+	 * are refused (dfb_region_size 0).
+	 */
 	index = of_property_match_string(dev->of_node, "memory-region-names",
 					 "framebuffer");
+	if (index == -ENODATA || index == -EINVAL) {
+		dcp->dfb_region_size = 0;
+		dev_info(dev, "no boot framebuffer\n");
+		goto clocks;
+	}
 	if (index < 0)
-		return -EINVAL;
+		return index;
 	fb = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "memory-region", index);
 	if (!fb)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -5168,6 +5180,7 @@ static int dcp_firmware_metadata_v27(struct apple_dcp *dcp)
 	if (!dcp->dfb_region_size)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+clocks:
 	clocks = of_property_count_u32_elems(dev->of_node, "apple,clock-ids");
 	if (clocks == -ENODATA &&
 	    of_property_present(dev->of_node, "apple,clock-ids"))
